{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"═══ ARCHAEOLOGY SETTLES IT: Pass-1 DID generate findings on OPUS until 2026-06-27, and the downgrade\nto sonnet is a five-week-old REGRESSION — not a design choice. This reframes the fix entirely. ═══\n\nI previously wrote on this ticket that the mitigation was to raise the rung from `trivial` to\n`standard`, on the reasoning that sonnet was \"where it runs today\". **That was wrong.** Sonnet is\nitself the result of an unnoticed regression, so preserving it would ratify the bug. Corrected below\nwith the evidence.\n\n**THE EMPIRICAL RECORD.** 3,843 plan-review `REVIEW_RESULT` sidecars in `.tickets-tracker`, aggregated\nby the recorded `data.model`, bucketed by day:\n\n    day           opus   sonnet\n    2026-06-24      16        0\n    2026-06-25      32        0\n    2026-06-26      25        0\n    2026-06-27      42        0     <- `_verifier_cfg` lands this day\n    2026-06-28      37       20     <- transition\n    2026-06-29       0       87     <- opus GONE\n    2026-06-30       0       78\n    ...              0      ...     (never returns; 2,710 sonnet runs since)\n\n115 opus runs before the change, ZERO after. A total, permanent changeover one day after the commit.\n\n**THE CAUSE.** `4beec08a4` (2026-06-27, \"verifier model downgrade in the workflow path\", WS2\ngawky-koi-grain) introduced `_verifier_cfg` to run **Pass-2 verify and Pass-4 coach** on the decisive\nnon-frontier model. Its own docstring asserts: *\"The Pass-1 finder is unaffected: it runs the YAML\n`model_ladder` via the ProductionBatchRunner, not `cfg.model`.\"*\n\nThat claim was false from the moment it was written, for a reason nobody could see at the time:\n`_verifier_cfg(cfg)` is passed as the **whole run's** cfg at the `produce_plan_review_verdict`\nboundary (`plan_review/__init__.py:605-607`), so `gate_dispatch` builds the RUNNER from the\ndowngraded cfg — and `PydanticAIRunner.run` then **discarded `req.config`**, throwing away the batch's\nladder rung and using the runner's downgraded config instead. So Pass-1 silently inherited a downgrade\naimed at Pass-2/Pass-4.\n\n**WHAT THIS MEANS FOR b690 — it is the ENABLER, not the cause.** Without b690, NO ladder rung can\ninfluence Pass-1 at all, because `req.config` is discarded before it is read. b690 is what makes the\ndeclaration reachable for the first time. The remaining problem is only that the declaration says\n`trivial`.\n\n**SO THE FIX IS A RESTORATION, and the correct rung is `frontier`:**\n\n    b690 (honour req.config)  +  plan-review.yaml model_ladder[0] = frontier\n      => Pass-1 generates findings on opus, as it did before 2026-06-27\n      => and `_verifier_cfg`'s docstring claim finally becomes TRUE\n\n`standard` would freeze the regression. `trivial` would deepen it. Only `frontier` restores the\nbehaviour that produced 115 recorded reviews, and it is the only option that is a preservation rather\nthan a new judgement about how strong a finder should be.\n\n**A SEPARATE UNTHREADED SEAM, found in the same trace and NOT covered by this ticket or by 7761.**\n`sizing.MODEL_LADDER` still hardcodes BARE Anthropic ids (`claude-haiku-4-5` 200k /\n`claude-sonnet-4-6` 1M / `claude-opus-4-8` 1M), and `models_at_or_above` returns them, so\n`sizing.py:424` does `replace(cfg, model=<bare claude-* id>)` on every context-limit escalation.\n**Escalation therefore bypasses the model-class table entirely** — on a Bedrock-configured run, an\nescalating Pass-1 criterion silently jumps to direct Anthropic. That is the same defect class as the\nepic's founding symptom (41 of 42 calls to direct Anthropic) and it is still live. Filing separately.\n\nAlso worth noting for whoever sets the rung: with rung 0 at `frontier`, `models_at_or_above(opus)`\nreturns just `[opus]`, so escalation becomes a no-op — which costs nothing, because sonnet and opus\nhave the SAME 1M window. The only size-meaningful step in that ladder was ever haiku→sonnet, and the\ngenuinely useful size handling (batch → one-criterion-per-call → the P8 too-big finding) is\nindependent of the model rungs."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785637337984736001,"uuid":"6c40a8ab-13e1-40db-8855-64c48c160823"}